art/models.json:
{
 "formatVersion": 1,
 "_note": "Model files for the web client, download zips and Unity (P7.7, plan-5 additions item 6). Paths are relative to the ThirdParty folder, forward slashes, exact case. A building type maps to a family through Data/catalog/models.json (baseFamily, variantFamilies); buildings[family].tiers[low|basic|premium].files lists the main body first, then details. Anything not mapped, or a mapped file that is missing on disk, falls back to the code-made shape, so a missing file never blocks a screen. Sizes ending in U are raw model units read from accessor bounds by Tools/art/gltf_bounds.py, not meters: each pack has its own unit, so multiply by that pack's metersPerUnit (packs) to get meters. buildings[family].fit says how the files meet the placed rect (stretch, tile or place) and each tier's scale line spells it out. deps lists the buffers and textures each model loads; ship them with it, and a model with a missing dep falls back. Generated by Tools/art/build_models.py, do not hand edit.",
 "fallbackShape": "code_box",
 "floorHeightM": {
  "value": 3.5,
  "source": "A",
  "why": "One floor of a stretched building body: between a 3 m home floor and a 4 m shop floor."
 },
